# The Eyes Have It: A Problem-Based Learning Exercise in Molecular Evolution

**Authors:** White, Harold B.

## Abstract
Molecular evolution provides an interesting context in which to use problem-based learning because it integrates a variety of topics in biology, biochemistry, and molecular biology. This three-stage problem for advanced students deals with the structure, multiple functions, and properties of lactate dehydrogenase isozymes, and the related evolutionary trade offs of gene sharing "versus" gene duplication among their corresponding genes. It has directive elements that require students to find and read classic articles, review thermodynamic principles, and apply their understanding to a mythical world wherein dinosaurs continued to evolve. The science fiction writing assignment that brings closure to the problem transformed the problem with respect to student interest and engagement. (Contains 1 table.)

